id: pm-7ivxas
title: "Identity refusal table omits linked-test updated_by and plan step owner, so those identity locations still accept URL userinfo"
description: "Found by the Codex review of PR 1714 (final round). After pm-ziv9yb, the URL-userinfo identity refusal judges the top-level author, assignee and claim_principal and a declared table of nested identity paths (comments, notes, learnings, dependencies, plan_decisions and plan_discoveries author, and the linked-test provenance author). Two identity locations in src/types.ts are not in the table: a linked test's updated_by (the author of its most recent metadata edit) and a plan step's owner. Both were unchecked before PR 1714 as well, so this is a gap in coverage rather than a regression. A runtime or registered field mapped onto tests or plan_steps can therefore store one of those identities with URL userinfo. Fix: add both entry paths to the declared table and pin them in the url-credentials spec."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: identity,redaction,runtime-fields,security
created_at: "2026-11-12T21:14:03.364Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-12T23:24:19.593Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-12T23:24:19.561Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-12T23:24:19.561Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: A tests entry updated_by or a plan_steps entry owner carrying URL userinfo is refused naming its entry path; The url-credentials spec pins both paths next to the existing declared paths
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
resolution: "The declared identity table now includes plan_steps owner and the linked-test updated_by, so a runtime or registered field mapped onto plan_steps or tests cannot store either identity with URL userinfo; the refusal names the entry path, such as tests[1].updated_by."
expected_result: Every identity location in the item types is judged
actual_result: url-credentials spec pins both new paths beside the existing ones; 57 related tests pass
